      "findings": [
        "S2 MINOR: 01-PRD lists ten must-have features against S2's 3-6 bar. reference/G G.2.1 (B5) raises the cap to 6-10 when a companion document is supplied, and this task ships a 3,896-line PRD; every added feature carries a grader. S2's bar is superseded for companion-backed tasks.",
        "S5 MINOR: 04-uiux carries no hex palette, no pixel type scale and no millisecond motion values. S5 predates the settled number rule (generate_instruction.md 'The number rule, DECIDED', A5, and tools/source_lint.py), which forbids a hex or a duration anywhere in the brief and carries colour as family, tone and shade. The uiux brief states every axis; it states them as words.",
        "S6 MINOR: 05-schema states the no-overlap invariant as an observable property of the stored data rather than as a named index or constraint. INV9 and G43 forbid naming the storage construct downstream, and the spec doc is written to the same register so the brief cannot inherit a mechanism from it.",
        "B1 MINOR: the booking-scheduling row gives one baseline role, `user`; this task declares `guest` and `host`. The idea and the companion both name two actors with different permission shapes, and a two-sided marketplace with one role cannot express the row-level scope the companion requires. Recorded in 00-decisions.md."
      ]
    },
