      "findings": [
        "A1 MINOR: `## Build plan` is absent. generate_instruction.md 2.1 removes it from the baseline emission, and reference/G G.3 adds the optional unbudgeted `## Front-end specification`, which this brief carries. Ten H2s are present and canonically spelled.",
        "A8 MINOR: the brief names `PENDING_HOLD_TTL_SEC` and `QUOTE_TTL_SEC`, which are outside A8's canon list. reference/J J.9 mandates exactly this shape for a timed hold: the human duration and the variable NAME are pinned in the brief, the production value sits in [environment].env and the verifier overrides the same variable. Both are read from the environment and neither is hardcoded.",
        "B1 MINOR: roles are `guest` and `host` against the row's single `user`. Same deviation as QC_spec B1, recorded in 00-decisions.md.",
        "B2 MINOR: the critical focus is present as numbered rule 25 with its negative case, and it deliberately omits the variant-a reminder clause. generate_instruction.md 4 deletes that clause at variant b and above, where the trap is what is being measured; this bundle is variant b.",
        "B3 MINOR: two of the three levers are present. generate_instruction.md 2.1 makes `## Build plan` non-baseline, so a baseline brief carries two by design.",
        "C5 MINOR, two parts. Rating aggregates are stored rather than computed on read, which the companion requires in as many words. Concurrency invariants are stated as observable properties rather than named storage constructs, which INV9 and G43 require of `## Data model`.",
        "C7 MINOR: `## Core features` runs well past the judge's 2,500-character slice. window_lint.py reports length and fails nothing, generate_instruction.md 4 says plainly not to cut a real rule to fit, and judge_score never touches reward. The companion states more graded rules than the window holds."
      ]
